# Close the application's side fully, let the testbench acknowledge the FIN without closing its
# own, then send data. RFC 2525 2.16, failure to send a RST after a half-duplex close: no
# application can read the data any more, so the DUT resets the connection.
scenario rfc2525-data-after-close
refs: RFC 2525 2.16, RFC 9293 3.6

listen l 8307
connect p l 8307 syn=opts_standard()
close p.conn
await p 1s match=is_fin(s) -> f
require fin f.ok
  what: Close sends a FIN
  got: {seg_desc(f)}
set p.rcv_nxt = f.seq + f.seq_len
send_ack p
send_data p "late"
# await looks only at this connection's four-tuple, the FIN_WAIT_2 one
await p 1s match=is_rst(s) -> r
check rst r.ok
  what: RFC 2525 2.16: data for a closed application draws a RST
  got: {seg_desc(r)}
if r.ok
  check rst.seq r.seq == p.rcv_nxt
    what: the RST carries SND.NXT, past the FIN, as RFC 9293 3.10.7.4 asks for a segment that acknowledges it
    got: {yes_no(r.seq == p.rcv_nxt, "SND.NXT", "another number")}
end
